through you Mr mayor um what I basically shared with uh city council member just for everybody's information tonight um was kind of the need for administrative inspection warrants in the fire service um this goes back to some US Supreme Court rulings um and where warrantless searches were actually done um and all those court cases were inadmissible the evidence was inadmissible um so just trying to provide a clear operational policy for our folks um what these two things basically does is um provide for fire code inspections um under the international fire code uh 2024 which is adopted by this governing body um we want to enter commercial occupancies um to do those regularly scheduled um fire inspections um

those are routine we do follow-up inspections um we gain consent from the business owners to come on their property we work with business owners while we walk their property um that's a pretty uh typical uh interaction for our fire service folks um there are some times though where we are denied entry to certain parts of a building um for for whatever reason they're they're worried about security or proprietary information things like that and um we continue to work through those conflicts with the business owners as we as we can um if we can't work through that conflict um basically we're stuck and we can't fulfill the need of our fire code um what state statute tells us as far as what we need to do to inspect those buildings um

just for everybody's information we do not inspect residential properties unless we are invited to do a home safety inspection but that is not enforceable by our fire code either it's just guidance um for somebody's home um the second aspect of this is our fire investigations uh those are very complex uh things that we have to to work through sometimes we don't know where the property owner is we can't find them um to finish out some of these uh investigations so um often when the property owners are there and they show up they want us to investigate the fire um we get um consent to investigation form signed and work with the property owners continually for sometimes weeks and

months to try to determine what caused a fire work with insurance companies everything so um but sometimes we can't find property owners um and so at that point we're also kind of stuck once the emergency uh ends and we leave that property we can no longer go back to said property um without some type of tool such as this administration inspection warrant to complete that out if we if we can't find the person if we can't gain their consent so um that's just the the few things I provided there obviously this has to go before a judge if we're going to request this we have to have a purpose um administrative probable cause it's just if we find something criminal in nature with a fire investigation we already pause back up and

